# All six classes were read once from this published mesh: step 0, sliver 5, ceiling 4, slope 0, thin 20, ledge 1.
# Thin and ledge remain rankings. These answers cover geometry and print intent; physical release, support removal, finish, strength and lifetime are unmeasured.

[sliver] The 1.2 mm top strip is the edge of the local flute backing pad. The backing is joined continuously to the enclosing wall and supplies the additional stock needed for the 1.2 mm deep source grooves, retaining 3 mm behind their deepest section. Its exposed edge width is not a freestanding wall thickness.
alternatives: A 4.2 mm flank throughout the body removes this local pad end but adds stock outside the texture field and narrows the cavity. Extending the backing above Z21 adds material beyond the selected 15 mm high flute field and changes the inner crown boundary.
