[ceiling] These are the fixed capture-lip undersides at Z7.40. The body-only lint omits the moving shoulders whose tops are Z6.92, so their model-to-model release air is 0.48 mm, not the reported 4.3 mm drop to the fixed floor. Each lip has 3 mm stock up to Z10.40 and is rooted on its 3 mm guide wall. The native project preserves the central release windows. Remove all automatic supports from the empty travel spaces before assessing motion; physical cleanup and release remain unmeasured.
alternatives: A corbel under a lip consumes the release air or the moving stroke. Thickening a lip upward adds material without changing its first release layer. Increasing Z air changes the local fit and belongs to a separate whole-object print.
