[ceiling] This is the lower cut face of the native front crown at Z13.556. The all-width fore clearance ends at Y6; the crown retains its inward 3 mm offset and source display profile above that cut. Automatic support decisions are retained for the flat underside. It is exposed along the fore cut and through the rear opening above the guide; the 3.156 mm fore reveal is a viewing allowance, and removal effort remains a physical result.
alternatives: A sloped replacement changes the native crown's lower section and the support interface. Filling downward to the fixed guide closes the fore reveal and adds stock outside the selected surface readings. Additional stock above this face does not improve deposition on its first underside layer.
